---
# An Atom feed of the recipes.
#
# jekyll-feed is still in the plugin list and still writes the <link rel=
# "alternate"> in <head> via {% feed_meta %}, but it no longer generates this
# file: its generator skips any feed path that already exists in the source,
# which is exactly what this is. That seam is why the plugin stays — the
# alternative was configuring `feed.collections.recipes.path: /feed.xml`, and
# that breaks. The plugin always builds a feed for `posts` too, this site has
# no _posts, and `feed_meta` advertises whatever `feed.path` is — which tracks
# posts, not collections. So the config route either collides two generated
# pages on /feed.xml or points autodiscovery at the empty one.
#
# Before this file the feed had zero entries for the same underlying reason:
# the plugin feeds `posts`, and every recipe is a collection document.
layout: null
sitemap: false
---
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom">
  {%- assign recipes = site.recipes | sort: "date" | reverse -%}
  {%- assign limit = site.feed.posts_limit | default: 20 -%}

  <generator uri="https://jekyllrb.com/" version="{{ jekyll.version }}">Jekyll</generator>
  <link href="{{ '/feed.xml' | absolute_url }}" rel="self" type="application/atom+xml" />
  <link href="{{ '/' | absolute_url }}" rel="alternate" type="text/html" />
  <id>{{ '/feed.xml' | absolute_url }}</id>
  <title type="html">{{ site.title | smartify | xml_escape }}</title>
  <subtitle>{{ site.tagline | default: site.description | strip_newlines | strip | xml_escape }}</subtitle>

  {%- comment -%}
  Atom wants the feed's own last-changed time, not the build time. Using the
  newest recipe's date means a rebuild that changes nothing does not tell every
  reader the feed moved.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  {%- assign newest = recipes | first -%}
  <updated>{{ newest.date | default: site.time | date_to_xmlschema }}</updated>

  {%- comment -%}
  Named here but deliberately not in _config.yml as `author:`, which
  jekyll-seo-tag would turn into a schema.org Person. Atom requires an author
  the feed can fall back on, and the larder is the thing publishing.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <author><name>{{ site.title | xml_escape }}</name></author>

  {%- for recipe in recipes limit: limit %}
  {%- assign title = recipe.title | smartify | strip_html | normalize_whitespace | xml_escape %}
  <entry>
    <title type="html">{{ title }}</title>
    <link href="{{ recipe.url | absolute_url }}" rel="alternate" type="text/html" title="{{ title }}" />
    <published>{{ recipe.date | date_to_xmlschema }}</published>
    <updated>{{ recipe.last_modified_at | default: recipe.date | date_to_xmlschema }}</updated>
    <id>{{ recipe.id | absolute_url | xml_escape }}</id>

    {%- if recipe.description and recipe.description != empty %}
    <summary type="html"><![CDATA[{{ recipe.description | strip_html | normalize_whitespace }}]]></summary>
    {%- endif %}

    {%- comment -%}
    The headnote only — not the ingredients and method, which live in front
    matter rather than the body. Two reasons to leave them out: a reader that
    already has the whole recipe has no reason to open the page, and those
    fields are the structured data the recipe page and its schema own, so
    flattening them into feed HTML would be a second copy to keep true.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- capture body %}
      {%- if recipe.image %}<p><img src="{{ recipe.image | absolute_url }}" alt="{{ title }}" /></p>{% endif %}
      {{- recipe.content | strip -}}
    {%- endcapture %}
    {%- assign body = body | strip %}
    {%- if body != empty %}
    <content type="html" xml:base="{{ recipe.url | absolute_url | xml_escape }}"><![CDATA[{{ body }}]]></content>
    {%- endif %}

    {%- for tag in recipe.tags %}
    <category term="{{ tag | xml_escape }}" />
    {%- endfor %}

    {%- assign image = recipe.image.path | default: recipe.image %}
    {%- if image %}
    {%- unless image contains "://" %}{% assign image = image | absolute_url %}{% endunless %}
    <media:thumbnail xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" url="{{ image | xml_escape }}" />
    {%- endif %}
  </entry>
  {%- endfor %}
</feed>
